Licence history -- this directory was GPL-3.0 until 2026-09-17
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Earlier revisions of Nexus/UEFI/ were a derivative work of EfiGuard
(https://github.com/Mattiwatti/EfiGuard, GPL-3.0) and were distributed under
GPL-3.0 accordingly. That obligation was real and was met: the derivation was
declared, upstream was credited, and the modified files were listed as GPLv3
section 5(a) requires.

Every EfiGuard-derived file has since been replaced with an independent
implementation or removed outright:

  pe.c, pe.h                   -> NexusPe.c, NexusPe.h
  util.c, util.h               -> NexusUtil.c, NexusUtil.h
  ntdef.h                      -> NexusNt.h
  arc.h                        -> NexusArc.h
  X64/Cet.asm, X64/Cet.nasm    -> X64/NexusCet.asm, X64/NexusCet.nasm
  VisualUefi.c                 -> NexusVisualUefi.c
  PatchNtoskrnl.c              -> rewritten
  PatchWinload.c               -> rewritten
  PatchBootmgr.c               -> rewritten
  byte-signature scanning      -> NexusPgLocate.c, NexusBootLocate.c
  inline hooking               -> NexusHook.c
  loader-block helpers         -> NexusLoaderBlock.c
  the DSE bypass and the
  SetVariable kernel R/W
  backdoor                     -> removed; neither is used

The driver protocol GUID was reissued at the same time, because an inherited
identifier is inherited regardless of what the code behind it says.

VERSIONS THIS APPLIES TO. Releases up to and including v2.0.0-alpha.4 contain
EfiGuard-derived code and remain licensed under GPL-3.0; nothing here withdraws
or alters the rights granted with them. v2.0.0-beta.1 and later contain no
derivative code and are Apache-2.0.

